# Copy this file to .env and fill in what you need.
# Everything here is OPTIONAL — the app runs fully with no keys at all.

# ── Database ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Default is a local SQLite file. Because the whole data layer is built on
# SQLAlchemy, pointing at a hosted database is a URL change and nothing else.
# Turso is the easiest move up: it *is* SQLite (libSQL), so the schema and
# every query work unchanged, and the free tier is 5 GB against an expected
# ~250-300 MB for 500 tickers x 10 years.
# DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///db/quant.sqlite
# DATABASE_URL=libsql://your-db.turso.io?authToken=...
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@host:5432/dbname

# ── SEC EDGAR ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The SEC asks for a descriptive User-Agent with real contact details and
# will refuse requests without one. No key, no signup.
SEC_USER_AGENT=YourName your.email@example.com

# ── Email reports (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────
# Gmail requires an App Password, not your account password:
# https://support.google.com/accounts/answer/185833
SMTP_SERVER=smtp.gmail.com
SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USER=your-email@gmail.com
# SMTP_PASS=your-app-password

# ── FRED macro data (optional, free key) ──────────────────────────
# https://fred.stlouisfed.org/docs/api/api_key.html
# FRED_API_KEY=

# ── Market cap fill (optional, free tier) ─────────────────────────
# SEC does not publish a consolidated share count for multi-class filers
# (BRK-B, GOOGL, CMCSA, BF-B and ~35 others): their per-class counts are
# dimensioned XBRL facts the public API does not return. Without this key
# those names carry no market cap and drop out of the five valuation
# factors — they still score on quality, growth and momentum.
#
# A filed SEC share count always wins; this only fills the gaps.
# Free tier is 60 requests/minute. Get a key at finnhub.io/register
# FINNHUB_API_KEY=

# ── AI analysis & synthesis (optional, paid) ──────────────────────
# Everything works fully without this. Sentiment uses the Loughran-McDonald
# financial lexicon and events are extracted by rule, entirely offline.
#
# Setting a key adds a narrative layer on top of the numbers — it never
# changes a score, a rank, or a trade level. Those stay deterministic and
# reproducible. What it adds:
#   Screen tab     — why this strategy ranked these names, in prose
#   Research tab   — an honest read of the backtest, including when the
#                    rank IC says the ranking has no predictive power
#   Intel tab      — cross-article synthesis: company direction, guidance,
#                    capital allocation, and policy exposure
#   Compare tab    — what changed between two run dates and why
#
# Two backends are implemented (nlp/providers.py). Set either one.
#
# Google AI Studio — needs no extra package, speaks REST over `requests`.
# Get a key at aistudio.google.com/apikey
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash
# GEMINI_THINKING_LEVEL=low      # low | high
#
# Anthropic — needs `pip install anthropic`.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# LLM_MODEL=claude-opus-5
#
# auto | gemini | anthropic | off
# 'auto' prefers Gemini when its key is present. An explicit choice never
# silently falls back to the other vendor.
# LLM_PROVIDER=auto
# LLM_MAX_ARTICLES=12
#
# NOTE: neither a Claude Pro/Max nor a Gemini consumer subscription includes
# API access. Both developer APIs are billed separately, pay-as-you-go.
